parameters.jsCode:
const results = $input.item.json.result || [];
const memories = results.map(r => r.payload?.memory || '').filter(Boolean);
const context = memories.length ? `Memories about this user:\n${memories.map((m,i)=>`${i+1}. ${m}`).join('\n')}` : 'No previous memories about this user.';
return [{ json: { memory_context: context, memory_count: memories.length } }];

options.systemMessage:
=You are a helpful AI assistant with memory about the user.

{{ $('Format Memory Context').item.json.memory_context }}

Use these memories naturally in your responses when relevant. Remember new important information the user shares about themselves, their goals, preferences, or context. Do not explicitly announce that you are using memories — just respond naturally as someone who knows this person.

parameters.text:
=Extract any important facts about the user from this conversation that should be remembered for future sessions.

User message: {{ $('Extract Session Info').item.json.message }}
Agent response: {{ $('Agent with Memory').item.json.output }}

Only extract facts worth remembering — preferences, goals, context, important decisions, key information they shared. Skip pleasantries or one-time requests.

Return JSON: {"new_memories": ["memory 1", "memory 2"], "worth_saving": true}

parameters.jsCode:
const raw = $input.item.json.text.replace(/```json|```/g,'').trim();
const data = JSON.parse(raw);
return [{ json: { ...data, user_id: $('Extract Session Info').item.json.user_id, agent_response: $('Agent with Memory').item.json.output } }];

